{"repositoryId":1423432741,"availability":"available","full":"Dnaltroc/PSEUDO-CEO","name":"PSEUDO-CEO","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-17T14:49:20Z","updated":"2026-10-19T15:40:35Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pseudo-ceo.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://pseudo-ceo.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T15:56:29.528Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T15:56:29.528Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T15:56:29.528Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T15:56:29.528Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A CEO strategy game built on real company data. You take over a struggling Fortune 500 company, make quarterly decisions, and see how your results compare with what the real leadership did.","Before Quarter 1 the player reads a one-page briefing in plain English on why the company is struggling. Each company has five or fewer points (STORY in src/ui.js), each linked to a source taken from the company's facts and five-forces evidence links in src/engine.js. The page ends with the decision the player is about to face."],"features":["This replaced the old Strategy room (Porter's Five Forces and a strategic posture). The strategy code in the engine is still there but unused. New games carry no strategy.","The server still accepts a strategy when a game started before the change sends one, so those runs replay to the score the player saw."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Dnaltroc/PSEUDO-CEO/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4707762f397c06296e5d04f289591039b8b815af02a254116efa903683625f14","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T15:56:29.663Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T15:56:29.663Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A CEO strategy game built on real company data. You take over a struggling Fortune 500 company, make quarterly decisions, and see how your results compare with wha